 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey, how are you doing?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.56,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_01"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm great, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.74,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_08"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I sit at a desk all day and my back is killing me. Are there exercises that help?",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.26,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes. Bridges, bird dogs and gentle cat cow stretches strengthen and loosen your back. A few minutes a day helps.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.86,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "What's a bird dog?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.03,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "On your hands and knees, you stretch one arm forward and the opposite leg back, hold for a few seconds, then switch.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.97,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Sounds doable. Should I also get a standing desk or",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 3.31,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "is that overrated?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.66,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It can help, but mostly by making you change position. Getting up and walking around every half hour matters more.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Alright, I'll set a reminder on my phone.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.72,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Good plan. And if the pain is sharp or doesn't improve, it's worth seeing a doctor.",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 1.02,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg2"
  }
 ]
}
